{title: There Is a Fountain}
{title_ko: 샘물과 같은 보혈은}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 258장}
{artist: William Cowper / Lowell Mason}
{genre: Easter}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
There is a [G]fountain filled with [C]blood
Drawn from Em[G]manuel's [D]veins
And sinners [G]plunged beneath that [C]flood
Lose all their [G]guilty [D]stains
Lose all their [G]guilty stains
Lose all their [C]guilty [G]stains
And sinners [G]plunged beneath that [C]flood
Lose all their [G]guilty [D]stains[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The dying [G]thief rejoiced to [C]see
That fountain [G]in his [D]day
And there may [G]I, though vile as [C]he
Wash all my [G]sins a[D]way
Wash all my [G]sins away
Wash all my [C]sins a[G]way
And there may [G]I, though vile as [C]he
Wash all my [G]sins a[D]way[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Dear dying [G]Lamb, Thy precious [C]blood
Shall never [G]lose its [D]power
Till all the [G]ransomed church of [C]God
Are saved to [G]sin no [D]more
Are saved to [G]sin no more
Are saved to [C]sin no [G]more
Till all the [G]ransomed church of [C]God
Are saved to [G]sin no [D]more[G]
{end_of_verse}
